A table whose name has spaces would go: the refusal writes the `-- @drop`
line with the name quoted, ready to paste.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE "dish of the day" (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO "dish of the day" VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `dish of the day` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its rows would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop table "dish of the day"` in schema.sql. Renamed? Drop it, and fill the new one from it: `-- @from table <new> = "dish of the day"`.
